WEBVTT

00:00:02.520 --> 00:00:04.020
Shugo, shugo!

00:00:04.020 --> 00:00:06.290
Start it off with a Doki! It's Shugo Chara time!

00:00:06.290 --> 00:00:10.330
In this episode, Ikuto and Tadase's past is revealed!

00:00:10.330 --> 00:00:13.110
And we might even find out the true identity of the school Chairman.

00:00:13.110 --> 00:00:15.570
So many mysteries will be unraveled!

00:00:15.570 --> 00:00:18.030
You don't mean our secrets, too?!

00:00:18.750 --> 00:00:20.460
Wait, we have secrets?

00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:22.590
Don't worry, just go with it!

00:00:22.590 --> 00:00:23.570
Doki!

00:00:35.140 --> 00:00:42.180
If you were to walk so the wind fluttered the edge of your cape,

00:00:42.180 --> 00:00:48.570
people would look up at you in quiet admiration.

00:00:48.820 --> 00:00:55.870
You can say spicy things like "it's not my style," if you want,

00:00:55.870 --> 00:01:02.290
but I know who you really are because I'm your friend!

00:01:02.290 --> 00:01:04.160
Stand! Bow!

00:01:04.160 --> 00:01:05.690
Nice and orderly now!

00:01:05.690 --> 00:01:09.530
And once that's done,

00:01:09.530 --> 00:01:14.800
it's time to start the school day.

00:01:15.130 --> 00:01:22.420
I like Mondays because I can see all my friends.

00:01:22.420 --> 00:01:28.820
There's nothing wrong with being abnormally happy.

00:01:28.820 --> 00:01:35.990
At lunch break, we have tea in the Royal Garden,

00:01:35.990 --> 00:01:43.330
where I tell you all my secrets!

00:01:56.190 --> 00:02:01.570
It was back during those peaceful days, when everyone was happy.

00:02:02.290 --> 00:02:04.720
Betty, that tickles!

00:02:05.260 --> 00:02:06.770
What's the meaning of this?

00:02:07.710 --> 00:02:11.200
How could he just disappear...

00:02:12.120 --> 00:02:13.690
What's he trying to do?

00:02:14.540 --> 00:02:17.450
Is he saying this is the end of our friendship?

00:02:20.250 --> 00:02:21.210
Is that you, Tadase?

00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:23.400
Come here.

00:02:24.220 --> 00:02:24.780
Okay.

00:02:28.920 --> 00:02:31.320
This is a very important key.

00:02:31.930 --> 00:02:35.010
I will give it to you, if you promise to take excellent care of it.

00:02:35.790 --> 00:02:38.090
Swear you won't lose it.

00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:38.930
Okay.

00:02:39.720 --> 00:02:44.180
You must never, ever break a promise. Understand?

00:02:44.880 --> 00:02:49.040
Don't become a person who shirks their responsibilities and runs off on their own.

00:02:50.020 --> 00:02:50.670
I won't.

00:02:52.420 --> 00:02:56.500
I was still so young that I couldn't understand what was going on.

00:02:57.320 --> 00:02:58.690
Except...

00:02:58.690 --> 00:03:01.170
That something had unquestionably broken.

00:03:01.170 --> 00:03:05.600
And I vaguely understood that those happy times would never return.

00:03:07.880 --> 00:03:09.890
Ikuto's father had disappeared,

00:03:10.190 --> 00:03:13.280
and his mother was hospitalized from the stress of it all.

00:03:13.760 --> 00:03:16.170
That much, I was able to understand.

00:03:16.740 --> 00:03:21.090
Episode 97
Tadase and Ikuto, The Horoscope of Fate!

00:03:23.530 --> 00:03:28.250
My family and Ikuto's had been close since the time we were very small.

00:03:29.280 --> 00:03:35.150
That was because when Ikuto and Utau's parents were away, our family would look after them.

00:03:36.380 --> 00:03:39.070
So you and Ikuto used to live together?

00:03:39.070 --> 00:03:41.920
This picture definitely makes it look like you got along well.

00:03:42.510 --> 00:03:45.100
Tadase always had a kingly aura, didn't he?

00:03:45.420 --> 00:03:46.600
Ikuto-nya...

00:03:46.600 --> 00:03:48.790
You weren't around then, Yoru?

00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:51.160
Nope. Was before I was born-nya.

00:03:51.450 --> 00:03:54.070
Ikuto-san's so cute!

00:03:54.070 --> 00:03:58.130
Really? I'd describe him as cool.

00:03:58.850 --> 00:04:02.050
Ikuto never spoke much after that.

00:04:02.760 --> 00:04:04.610
And he never smiled.

00:04:05.050 --> 00:04:07.430
But smiling is way more fun...

00:04:08.110 --> 00:04:10.410
Still, I loved him.

00:04:11.620 --> 00:04:13.250
My big brother, Ikuto...

00:04:15.440 --> 00:04:16.770
Over here, over here!

00:04:17.610 --> 00:04:20.900
This is Brother and Uta... Uta...

00:04:21.370 --> 00:04:22.820
Utan's room!

00:04:22.820 --> 00:04:23.910
U-ta-u!

00:04:23.910 --> 00:04:25.910
Don't treat us like monkeys.

00:04:25.910 --> 00:04:27.320
We're happy to have you with us.

00:04:27.790 --> 00:04:30.590
Please make yourselves right at home.

00:04:33.590 --> 00:04:35.910
I'll unpack your things into the bureau.

00:04:36.220 --> 00:04:37.150
It's okay.

00:04:38.240 --> 00:04:39.790
We'll handle it ourselves.

00:04:39.790 --> 00:04:41.580
O-Oh...

00:04:43.480 --> 00:04:44.410
A violin?

00:04:48.090 --> 00:04:51.100
What's with the long face?

00:04:52.700 --> 00:04:55.170
Are you uneasy about them living with us?

00:04:55.170 --> 00:04:56.660
It's not that...

00:04:56.660 --> 00:04:58.020
Mizue-san.

00:04:58.630 --> 00:05:00.460
It has begun to rain.

00:05:00.460 --> 00:05:01.550
Mother!

00:05:02.240 --> 00:05:05.830
I will handle this here. Tend to the laundry.

00:05:06.560 --> 00:05:08.830
Certainly. Thank you, Mother.

00:05:14.060 --> 00:05:19.230
When I think back, I can see that the gears had already begun to turn.

00:05:20.620 --> 00:05:23.320
But I was happy.

00:05:24.450 --> 00:05:28.460
I suddenly had siblings and we had fun every day.

00:05:29.300 --> 00:05:32.970
7... 8... 9, 10!

00:05:34.950 --> 00:05:36.980
It sucks being "it."

00:05:37.500 --> 00:05:41.300
Tadase's a shrimp, and it's hard to sense Ikuto.

00:05:42.460 --> 00:05:45.110
Betty, knock that off!

00:05:45.590 --> 00:05:47.070
Found you, Tadase.

00:05:47.070 --> 00:05:48.500
Is it over?

00:05:48.940 --> 00:05:52.250
Ikuto! I found you!

00:05:52.250 --> 00:05:54.830
Brother, you're really good at hide-and-seek!

00:05:56.230 --> 00:05:58.070
Ikuto!

00:05:58.070 --> 00:06:02.770
When Utau's "it," I somehow get really stoked about hiding.

00:06:03.960 --> 00:06:05.750
Hey, hurry up.

00:06:06.470 --> 00:06:08.170
Just a little, okay?

00:06:21.040 --> 00:06:23.730
Sometimes, we'd ask him to play the violin for us.

00:06:24.660 --> 00:06:29.200
It always put the most gentle look on his face.

00:06:33.150 --> 00:06:39.270
Wasn't his father, that man who went missing, a violinist?

00:06:39.270 --> 00:06:42.230
Correct. Tsukiyomi Aruto.

00:06:48.210 --> 00:06:51.390
I was too young to comprehend such adult matters,

00:06:52.270 --> 00:06:58.480
but we were always together, and I wished we could've stayed that way forever.

00:07:05.320 --> 00:07:08.370
Oh no, I broke it! What should I do?

00:07:08.730 --> 00:07:12.200
I pushed you, Tadase. I'll apologize.

00:07:12.530 --> 00:07:14.100
What happened here?

00:07:14.710 --> 00:07:15.830
Mommy...

00:07:16.310 --> 00:07:19.300
How many times have I told you not to run in the hall?

00:07:19.300 --> 00:07:21.720
For goodness' sake! Which one of you broke it?

00:07:22.860 --> 00:07:24.010
I did.

00:07:27.900 --> 00:07:30.510
I did it. Sorry.

00:07:33.700 --> 00:07:36.440
Don't fib, Brother! I did it!

00:07:36.440 --> 00:07:37.510
No, I...

00:07:38.560 --> 00:07:39.550
It doesn't matter. Hurry-

00:07:39.550 --> 00:07:41.010
Is there an issue?

00:07:41.010 --> 00:07:41.810
Mother!

00:07:47.700 --> 00:07:50.650
Bring a bucket filled with water and some old newspapers.

00:07:51.300 --> 00:07:53.110
We'll clean it up together.

00:07:53.520 --> 00:07:54.170
Yes, Ma'am.

00:07:57.770 --> 00:08:00.540
All things with form inevitably break.

00:08:01.110 --> 00:08:07.040
However, if you give it proper care, it will serve people well for a long time.

00:08:07.510 --> 00:08:10.740
That is what happiness means to such things.

00:08:10.740 --> 00:08:14.510
What's important is to have a caring heart.

00:08:15.080 --> 00:08:16.420
Do you understand?

00:08:16.820 --> 00:08:17.740
Yes.

00:08:20.040 --> 00:08:21.940
What a wonderful woman!

00:08:21.940 --> 00:08:30.730
Yes. But, to continue, my mother began to increasingly avoid Ikuto.

00:08:31.510 --> 00:08:33.750
Nothing to be done about that personality of his.

00:08:33.750 --> 00:08:37.200
He's been misunderstood his whole life-nya.

00:08:37.800 --> 00:08:39.640
And then what happened?

00:08:40.020 --> 00:08:41.610
I heard a rumor.

00:08:42.310 --> 00:08:43.080
A rumor?

00:08:43.800 --> 00:08:46.990
A rumor about Ikuto's missing father.

00:08:48.640 --> 00:08:50.550
A cursed violin?

00:08:51.140 --> 00:08:51.710
Right.

00:08:52.530 --> 00:08:55.530
All of the people who heard Tsukiyomi Alto play the violin

00:08:55.530 --> 00:08:58.050
either died or ended up in dire circumstances.

00:08:58.800 --> 00:09:01.080
That's nothing but superstition.

00:09:02.080 --> 00:09:03.270
Perhaps you're right...

00:09:03.860 --> 00:09:09.770
But when I look at him, he reminds me of a black cat of misfortune.

00:09:10.500 --> 00:09:16.510
His heart, so wounded from the disappearance of his father, can no longer trust in others.

00:09:17.250 --> 00:09:20.060
What will become of him if you, of all people, don't believe in him?

00:09:20.530 --> 00:09:23.320
But I'm afraid...

00:09:25.290 --> 00:09:26.230
Tadase-san.

00:09:28.240 --> 00:09:30.220
What do you think?

00:09:30.890 --> 00:09:32.960
Do you like Tsukiyomi Ikuto?

00:09:33.760 --> 00:09:34.860
Brother?

00:09:36.180 --> 00:09:36.950
I like him.

00:09:37.400 --> 00:09:40.480
I love him! I hope we're together forever!

00:09:40.820 --> 00:09:41.810
Tadase...

00:09:42.910 --> 00:09:44.680
Then, believe in him.

00:09:45.830 --> 00:09:46.350
I will!

00:09:47.040 --> 00:09:49.450
I'll believe in Brother!

00:09:50.820 --> 00:09:51.750
Ikuto?

00:09:53.110 --> 00:09:53.920
What's the matter?

00:10:03.630 --> 00:10:04.320
What is it?

00:10:05.440 --> 00:10:06.320
Nothing.

00:10:19.540 --> 00:10:20.500
Betty?

00:10:21.770 --> 00:10:25.240
Brother, where are you going?

00:10:29.760 --> 00:10:31.640
A violin for adults?

00:10:33.370 --> 00:10:34.570
Please, wait!

00:10:35.070 --> 00:10:36.420
Brother!

00:10:36.420 --> 00:10:37.080
Broth-

00:10:39.460 --> 00:10:40.410
Wait...

00:10:45.840 --> 00:10:47.160
Brother...

00:10:48.240 --> 00:10:49.650
Why?

00:10:52.700 --> 00:10:56.710
And I suddenly had no idea where he had gone.

00:10:59.060 --> 00:11:04.120
Shortly after, their mother, recently released from the hospital, came and took Utau away.

00:11:04.120 --> 00:11:07.260
And then she remarried Easter's Director?

00:11:07.720 --> 00:11:08.180
Right.

00:11:09.160 --> 00:11:12.340
Ever since then, I've waited for him, believing.

00:11:12.960 --> 00:11:18.950
But somewhere in my heart, I've always been desperate to know the reason why...

00:11:20.880 --> 00:11:22.290
And then, two years ago...

00:11:24.750 --> 00:11:25.710
I'm home.

00:11:29.680 --> 00:11:30.830
That sound...

00:11:33.000 --> 00:11:34.000
Brother!

00:11:55.500 --> 00:11:56.350
Betty!

00:11:58.010 --> 00:12:02.150
What's wrong?! Can you hear me? Betty! Betty!

00:12:04.330 --> 00:12:05.070
Betty...

00:12:10.550 --> 00:12:11.860
What did you do?

00:12:13.480 --> 00:12:16.490
What did you do to Betty, Brother?

00:12:20.760 --> 00:12:21.970
The Dumpty Key...

00:12:23.620 --> 00:12:26.860
That's something my father gave to me.

00:12:27.400 --> 00:12:29.640
Why do you have it?

00:12:30.250 --> 00:12:31.120
Why?

00:12:33.290 --> 00:12:36.000
Say something, Brother!

00:12:38.790 --> 00:12:41.030
Mother! Mother!

00:12:41.730 --> 00:12:43.650
Mother, please wake up!

00:12:45.170 --> 00:12:46.410
Grandmother?

00:12:51.120 --> 00:12:54.680
He really is a black cat that brings misfortune...

00:13:00.210 --> 00:13:01.080
Brother...

00:13:03.300 --> 00:13:04.530
Ikuto-niisan!

00:13:08.400 --> 00:13:12.700
Thankfully, Grandmother was treated quickly and her life was saved.

00:13:13.520 --> 00:13:15.020
But Betty did not fare as well.

00:13:15.800 --> 00:13:20.930
Even now, I don't know whether it was Tsukiyomi Ikuto's fault.

00:13:21.750 --> 00:13:26.190
But if it wasn't, I wish he would at least say so.

00:13:27.160 --> 00:13:30.690
Keeping silent this whole time is no different from running away.

00:13:31.960 --> 00:13:32.880
Running away...

00:13:33.770 --> 00:13:35.520
Could this explain his actions?

00:13:36.310 --> 00:13:40.740
If I could create a character like that, I might have it easier.

00:13:40.900 --> 00:13:44.590
I'm not going to do something you'd actually hate.

00:13:45.290 --> 00:13:47.720
If it was all on purpose...

00:13:48.310 --> 00:13:51.430
"Will you let me fall in love with you," was it?

00:13:52.780 --> 00:13:55.560
Quite a passionate confession for a little boy.

00:13:56.480 --> 00:14:01.980
If the "black cat of misfortune" is purposely trying to hurt people and make them hate him...

00:14:06.550 --> 00:14:07.700
Amu-chan?

00:14:15.070 --> 00:14:20.520
I know I lied to you, and that I hurt you.

00:14:20.890 --> 00:14:27.420
Hurting others is so sad and complicated, because it leaves scars on your heart, too.

00:14:28.320 --> 00:14:33.350
So if it's true that Ikuto has been hurting people on purpose...

00:14:34.500 --> 00:14:38.730
His heart must be worse off than anyone's!

00:14:39.650 --> 00:14:42.690
He must be in more pain than any of us!

00:14:50.720 --> 00:14:52.150
Amu-chan...

00:14:58.300 --> 00:15:00.790
This is terrible! I can't stand it!

00:15:01.640 --> 00:15:03.670
I've had enough!

00:15:06.150 --> 00:15:08.400
How long are we gonna be so glum?!

00:15:08.690 --> 00:15:12.140
I'm the baby here, so crying is <i>my</i> job!

00:15:12.450 --> 00:15:13.380
Yaya?

00:15:13.660 --> 00:15:15.100
She Character Changed.

00:15:15.100 --> 00:15:18.550
Can the weepy-weepy!

00:15:23.020 --> 00:15:24.750
What wind pressure!

00:15:24.750 --> 00:15:27.300
And she's flailing her legs faster than the eye can see...

00:15:27.300 --> 00:15:28.330
Amu-chi!

00:15:28.330 --> 00:15:29.050
Yes?

00:15:29.050 --> 00:15:31.300
You're the main character!

00:15:31.300 --> 00:15:33.340
You've got four Guardian Eggs!

00:15:33.340 --> 00:15:35.580
And you can do a lot of Character Transformations!

00:15:35.580 --> 00:15:38.910
So since you're the star, you've gotta overcome all this sad stuff!

00:15:39.200 --> 00:15:42.640
That's what happens in all of my anime and manga!

00:15:42.640 --> 00:15:44.830
You exterminate the bad guys, like "bam!"

00:15:44.830 --> 00:15:47.480
Then you save the captured kid lickety-split, patch everything up,

00:15:47.480 --> 00:15:50.050
and all the problems are solved in the end, no questions asked!

00:15:50.450 --> 00:15:53.800
That's the path the main character travels!

00:16:02.160 --> 00:16:04.960
I guess blurting out everything she had bottled up inside...

00:16:04.960 --> 00:16:06.570
...wiped her right out-dechu.

00:16:07.250 --> 00:16:10.950
You know what, Yaya, you're right.

00:16:10.950 --> 00:16:13.730
But it's not just me.

00:16:13.730 --> 00:16:17.030
Nagihiko, Rima, Tadase-kun, Yaya...

00:16:18.260 --> 00:16:19.500
And Ikuto, too...

00:16:21.090 --> 00:16:24.720
We're all the main characters of our own stories.

00:16:25.850 --> 00:16:28.250
Let's save Ikuto!

00:16:28.250 --> 00:16:31.200
Then everyone'll get their happy endings!

00:16:31.200 --> 00:16:32.400
Yeah!

00:16:32.400 --> 00:16:33.680
Yeah!

00:16:37.220 --> 00:16:39.590
Easy to say, but we have no idea where to go.

00:16:39.590 --> 00:16:42.750
Time to break into Easter, yeah!

00:16:42.750 --> 00:16:44.630
They chucked us out of there before, remember?

00:16:45.070 --> 00:16:48.940
Right! So we're fired up, but what should we do?

00:16:49.380 --> 00:16:50.670
This is a problem...

00:16:51.650 --> 00:16:54.410
Perhaps a certain someone could give us a little hint.

00:16:55.130 --> 00:16:56.530
Who do you mean?

00:16:56.970 --> 00:17:01.950
The Chairman, Founding King, and planetarium manager? That guy?

00:17:02.290 --> 00:17:03.710
Right, Tsukasa-san.

00:17:06.420 --> 00:17:07.290
Pardon us.

00:17:08.240 --> 00:17:09.680
Oh, he's not here.

00:17:09.930 --> 00:17:11.170
What should we do?

00:17:11.750 --> 00:17:12.650
Don't worry.

00:17:13.240 --> 00:17:14.930
He's usually...

00:17:25.460 --> 00:17:26.810
A hidden door?!

00:17:27.360 --> 00:17:29.330
What the heck?!

00:17:29.830 --> 00:17:32.360
People actually make stuff like this?!

00:17:32.730 --> 00:17:35.530
We've discovered yet another secret base!

00:17:35.530 --> 00:17:37.040
Let's check it out!

00:17:39.060 --> 00:17:39.640
Let's go.

00:17:39.640 --> 00:17:40.370
Yeah.

00:17:43.180 --> 00:17:47.880
My relatives, the Amakawas, have run this school for generations.

00:17:48.450 --> 00:17:51.700
But they've always been somewhat mysterious people.

00:17:51.700 --> 00:17:54.090
What secrets has he been keeping from the King?

00:17:54.090 --> 00:17:56.260
This is kinda fun-nya!

00:17:56.260 --> 00:17:57.780
This door won't open.

00:17:58.110 --> 00:17:59.220
It's a fake.

00:17:59.810 --> 00:18:01.830
This door opens, but...

00:18:01.830 --> 00:18:02.920
It's tiny!

00:18:02.920 --> 00:18:05.560
It's specially-made for Guardian Eggs.

00:18:05.560 --> 00:18:10.550
I don't think these tricks have any particular significance. They're just for "fun."

00:18:10.720 --> 00:18:11.940
A hobby?

00:18:11.940 --> 00:18:16.530
I can't believe there's an attraction like this under the school! This rocks!

00:18:16.790 --> 00:18:18.960
You're always looking on the bright side...

00:18:19.780 --> 00:18:21.800
Well, yeah. Something wrong with that?

00:18:21.800 --> 00:18:24.550
Nothing at all. It's what I like about you.

00:18:25.010 --> 00:18:27.190
I was actually a bit moved earlier.

00:18:27.700 --> 00:18:30.750
When? You mean when I was kicking my legs like crazy?

00:18:30.750 --> 00:18:35.540
Yeah. Who'd have thought the one to turn everyone's feelings around

00:18:35.540 --> 00:18:37.510
would be a girl like you.

00:18:39.510 --> 00:18:41.530
Yaya, we're going.

00:18:41.740 --> 00:18:44.170
Right. Wait!

00:18:49.710 --> 00:18:50.830
What is it?

00:18:50.830 --> 00:18:55.070
Nothing, I just have a good feeling about this.

00:18:55.550 --> 00:18:57.600
Of course, everything will be A-OK!

00:18:58.030 --> 00:19:00.740
'Cause you've got me with you!

00:19:02.580 --> 00:19:04.490
That's right. Let's go!

00:19:19.250 --> 00:19:21.430
My, what perfect timing.

00:19:22.200 --> 00:19:24.350
I just put the tea on.

00:19:24.930 --> 00:19:27.540
This is inside the planetarium.

00:19:27.540 --> 00:19:29.810
So that's where it connects to!

00:19:30.110 --> 00:19:32.050
Enough tea for everyone?

00:19:32.050 --> 00:19:35.050
I guess he was expecting us-dechu.

00:19:36.590 --> 00:19:39.320
Niboshi! Niboshi!

00:19:40.200 --> 00:19:42.200
I see... So that's it...

00:19:42.800 --> 00:19:47.040
I want to save Ikuto and ask him to tell me the truth.

00:19:47.040 --> 00:19:49.960
Including why he disappeared without saying a word.

00:19:50.550 --> 00:19:54.710
Oh, I wonder if I did a bad thing.

00:19:55.570 --> 00:20:01.180
I was the one who hid Ikuto when he first went missing.

00:20:06.520 --> 00:20:10.650
Ikuto-kun was stuck in a really bad predicament back then.

00:20:11.110 --> 00:20:14.770
He needed to get out of Easter's sight for a while.

00:20:15.300 --> 00:20:17.510
Why didn't you tell me?

00:20:17.510 --> 00:20:18.900
That's the question, isn't it?

00:20:18.900 --> 00:20:20.700
Yes, that <i>is</i> the question!

00:20:20.700 --> 00:20:23.280
Tadase's actually being the straight-man?

00:20:23.280 --> 00:20:25.070
Rare, but sharp.

00:20:25.420 --> 00:20:28.420
So, what really happened with Betty two years ago?

00:20:28.840 --> 00:20:30.260
And my grandmother?

00:20:30.260 --> 00:20:32.110
And my key?

00:20:33.250 --> 00:20:35.620
You certainly have a plethora of questions.

00:20:36.140 --> 00:20:39.840
But you must find the key to your story on your own.

00:20:40.650 --> 00:20:45.970
A fate yet undreamt shall come in time, though not revealed by horoscope.

00:20:45.970 --> 00:20:49.680
And those myriad falling stars are what make life so enjoyable.

00:20:50.280 --> 00:20:56.150
Right now, you are all trying to intercept a large meteor and change its orbit.

00:20:56.870 --> 00:20:58.760
Even I cannot predict the results.

00:20:59.170 --> 00:21:05.530
But what's most crucial is your desire to realize your dreams.

00:21:07.730 --> 00:21:12.260
I've arranged for someone to be at the school gates who may be of assistance.

00:21:12.260 --> 00:21:13.540
Someone that can help?

00:21:13.540 --> 00:21:16.400
Yes. And one more thing.

00:21:18.940 --> 00:21:20.000
That picture book...

00:21:20.690 --> 00:21:24.470
Libra's lucky item for this month is a picture book.

00:21:25.360 --> 00:21:26.950
Now everything's set.

00:21:28.520 --> 00:21:30.300
Thank you, Tsukasa-san!

00:21:36.560 --> 00:21:37.840
That picture book...

00:21:38.950 --> 00:21:43.170
Do you recall the page that was lost?

00:21:43.790 --> 00:21:45.090
You...

00:21:52.820 --> 00:21:56.420
He's out? If he's not here, then...

00:22:00.350 --> 00:22:03.540
I wanted to inform him that I think we'll have the Embryo soon.

00:22:04.660 --> 00:22:07.550
There will be problems if we let it slip away again.

00:22:08.260 --> 00:22:10.550
We've finally reached this stage...

00:22:11.260 --> 00:22:14.560
It won't be long now, Hikaru.

00:22:27.870 --> 00:22:33.220
You sure do seem determined.

00:22:34.630 --> 00:22:39.270
So even if you screw up, it'll somehow turn out all right.

00:22:39.970 --> 00:22:46.640
How about you just trust in yourself?

00:22:46.920 --> 00:22:53.100
Take that first step and everything will work out fine.

00:22:53.710 --> 00:23:00.030
Even if people see through your cool exterior, keep marching on.

00:23:00.450 --> 00:23:09.110
Look up at the blue sky and everything will reset!

00:23:09.690 --> 00:23:12.750
Take it easy! Take it easy!

00:23:13.030 --> 00:23:23.290
Try to relax those shoulders and clear your mind.

00:23:23.290 --> 00:23:30.000
The more you do it, the easier it'll get, so keep taking it easy.

00:23:30.000 --> 00:23:35.200
Ride the flow of time and you'll be...

00:23:36.260 --> 00:23:39.000
Shining! Shining! Shining!

00:23:50.540 --> 00:23:52.790
We have to save Ikuto.

00:23:52.790 --> 00:23:55.220
But we don't know where he is...

00:23:55.220 --> 00:23:57.910
Maybe some fortune-telling will help.

00:23:57.910 --> 00:24:01.740
If we use a radio, we might be able to hear Ikuto's violin!

00:24:01.740 --> 00:24:03.890
Right... Good idea...

00:24:03.890 --> 00:24:05.890
Hold on, that's so not true!

00:24:06.720 --> 00:24:08.930
But it might well be...

00:24:09.970 --> 00:24:12.160
Next time on Shugo Chara!! Doki:

00:24:12.160 --> 00:24:14.530
Reborn!! My Radiant Dancing Princess!

00:24:14.530 --> 00:24:16.760
She's finally come back to us!

00:24:16.760 --> 00:24:19.310
And we're coming for you, Ikuto!
